313 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/AP<</N 701 0 R>>/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/DA(0 0 0 rg /Helv 0 Tf)/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 8392704/M(D:20250930132510-06'00')/MK<<>>/NM(2d4fc23c-8dc2-472e-9983-a92152ff6bdb)/Rect[66.8084 66.723697 554.681 369.269]/T(Text Field22)/V(All the analysts involved in the testing - the initial prepping analyst \(Ishita Sharma\), the initial processing analyst \(Alex Saravia\), the initial reading analyst \(Elysse Nioupin\), the retest prepping and reading analyst \(Andrew Carrillo\), and the retest processing analyst \(Ayomide Odugbesi\) - were interviewed comprehensively. Their answers are recorded throughout this document. This investigation was performed in accordance with MICRO-SOP-53, Sterility Test Out-of-Specification Investigation Procedure.\r \rINITIAL TEST UNDER SUBMISSION ETX-260902-0505:\rAll analysts involved in the prepping, processing, and reading of the sample - Ishita Sharma, Alex Saravia, and Elysse Nioupin - were interviewed comprehensively. Their answers are recorded throughout this document. This investigation was performed in accordance with MICRO-SOP-53, Sterility Test Out-of-Specification Investigation Procedure.\r \rUpon arrival, the sample was stored refrigerated in accordance with the Client's instructions. Prepping analyst - Ishita Sharma - and processing analyst - Alex Saravia - verified the physical integrity and packaging of the sample throughout both the preparation and processing stages. No leaks, cracks, or visible turbidity were observed at any point, verifying container integrity.\r \rAll reagents and supplies mentioned in the material section above were stored according to the suppliers' recommendations, and their integrity was visually verified before utilization. Moreover, all reagents and supplies had valid expiration dates. The functionality of all equipment was confirmed by reviewing data generated by our comprehensive in-house continuous monitoring system.\r \rThe cleanroom suite \(CR 114\) used for processing procedures comprises three interconnected sections: the innermost ISO 7 cleanroom \(114B\), which connects to the middle ISO 7 buffer room \(114A\), and then to the outermost ISO 8 anteroom \(114\). A positive air pressure system is maintained throughout the suite to ensure controlled, unidirectional airflow from 114B through 114A and into 114.\r \rThe ISO 5 Biological Safety Cabinet \(BSC\) E001316, located in the innermost ISO 7 room \(114B\), was used for sample processing steps. It was thoroughly cleaned and disinfected prior to each procedure in accordance with MICRO SOP-9 \(Cleaning and Disinfecting Procedure for Microbiology\). Additionally, BSC E001316 was certified and approved by both the Engineering and Quality Assurance teams. Sample processing was conducted in the ISO 5 BSC E001316 in the innermost ISO 7 room \(114B\) by Alex Saravia on 04Sep26 as per MICRO-SOP-5 \(USP <71> / EP 2.6.1 Sterility Test\).)>>
endobj

